0Z_investigation_capability_taxonomy/`, PR #2337).\n\n## Goal\nAdd a `device.info` capability to `pkgs/id/src/world_caps.rs` returning the device's capability manifest (display kind/size/colours, input keys/encoder/pointer/text_entry, sensors with accuracy, audio in/out, transport class), so a world program can adapt one model to web, ESP32 and text/agent devices instead of rendering blind.\n\n## Why first\nEvery other interface capability in the taxonomy is conditional on it. It is deliberately a capability, not a surface field, so a program asks when it cares.\n\n## Scope\n- New catalog name `device.info` (append-only CATALOG rule; existing 17 names unchanged; no `WANTS_VERSION` bump — v1 already admits new names).\n- Manifest value shape per taxonomy §3.1: `{manifest:{v:1}, display, input, sensors, audio, network}`.\n- One-shot request only; the manifest is node-local, journaled, unsigned — same trust rule as other grants.\n- Per-device caching by the adapter; a program must never be able to make the device re-enumerate for free.\n- Refusal: `unknown_cap` if the node cannot describe itself.\n\n## Acceptance\n- `device.info` in CATALOG, provider in the world actor, and a test asserting the manifest round-trips and that an unknown manifest version is refused.\n- Program-side helper (Roc or plain JSON) documented in the module header alongside the existing wants example.\n- No change to existing capability semantics.\n\n## Out of scope\n`form.*`, `loc.*`, `media.*` (separate follow-ups), MQTT transport (separate follow-up).\n\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `device.info` is in the world_caps CATALOG (append-only; existing 17 names unchanged, no WANTS_VERSION bump) with a provider in the world actor\n- [ ] A test asserts the manifest round-trips and that an unknown manifest version is refused (`unknown_cap` when the node cannot describe itself)\n- [ ] Program-side helper (Roc or plain JSON) documented in the module header alongside the existing wants example\n- [ ] No change to existing capability semantics; per-device adapter caching means a program cannot force free re-enumeration\n","closed_by":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/2338/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/2338/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}